<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">NOTES:      1)The aforesaid consol financial results of IL&amp;FS Investment Managers Ltd (Holding Co), its subsidiaries (Holding Co &amp; its subsidiaries together constitute the Group) &amp; jointly controlled entities for qtr &amp; nine mths ended Dec 31, 2022 along-with comparative period have been reviewed by AC &amp; subsequently approved by BOD of Company at its meeting held on Feb 13, 2023  in terms of Reg 33 of the SEBI LODR, 2015. Financial results for qtr &amp; nine mths ended Dec 31, 2022 have been subjected to LR by Stat Auditors of Company      2)Financial results have been prepared in accordance with recognition &amp; measurement principles laid down in Ind AS 34 – Interim Financial Reporting, notified under Sec 133 of the Companies Act 2013 read with Companies (Ind AS) Rules 2015, as amended from time to time &amp; other accounting principles generally accepted in India      3)As per requirements of Ind AS 108 - Operating Segments, based on evaluation of financial information for allocation of resources &amp; assessing performance, the Group has identified a single segment i.e. providing asset management services &amp; other related services. As such, there are no separate reportable business or geographical segments as per Ind AS 108      4)MCA, Govt of India, has vide its letter dtd Oct 1, 2018 initiated investigation by SFIO against Infrastructure Leasing &amp; Financial Services Ltd (IL&amp;FS), the Holding Co &amp; its subsidiaries (including the Group) under Sec 212(1) of the Companies Act, 2013. On Dec 3, 2018, MCA on the directions of the NCLT, Mumbai has impleaded various Group Companies of IL&amp;FS (which includes the Group) as Respondents to the Petition filed by them on Oct 1, 2018. Further based on another petition of the MCA under Sec 130 (1) of the Companies Act, 2013, NCLT has, on Jan 1, 2019, ordered re-opening of books of accounts for the past FY 2012-13 to FY 2017-18 of IL&amp;FS ( Ultimate Holding Co), IL&amp;FS Financial Services Ltd (IFIN a fellow subsidiary) &amp; IL&amp;FS Transportation Networks Ltd (ITNL a fellow subsidiary). While the Group, based on its current understanding, believes that above would not have material impact on financial results, the implications, if any, arising from aforesaid developments would be known only after aforesaid matters are concluded &amp; hence are not determinable at this stage      5)The term of most of the existing funds being managed/advised by the Group has already been over. Other funds being managed/advised by the Group are approaching end of their term in near future which has resulted/is likely to result in significant reduction in the Group’s fee revenue. Mgmt expects that its future income from existing funds being managed/advised together with liquid assets held by the Group as at Dec 31, 2022 will be adequately sufficient to meet the Group 's existing &amp; future obligations arising over the next 12 months      Meanwhile IL&amp;FS Board has been working on a resolution plan, with aview to enable value preservation for stakeholders of IL&amp;FS Group. Resolution plan, inter alia, involves sale of assets/businesses/companies owned by IL&amp;FS. And in this regard, IL&amp;FS Board has on Dec 21, 2018 &amp; Sept 27, 2019 invited public Expression of Interest (EoI) for sale of its entire stake in the Company. Accordingly, Company’s plans for new fund raise have been kept on hold pending completion of stake sale. Further, with outbreak of pandemic timelines for sale process have got delayed &amp; while there is material uncertainty with regard to stake sale, mgmt believes that use of going concern assumption for preparation of these financial results is appropriate      7)The financial stat of its subsidiary IIML Fund Managers (Singapore) Pte Ltd &amp; its Joint Ventures IL&amp;FS Milestone Realty Advisors Pvt Ltd and Standard Chartered IL&amp;FS Management (Singapore) Pte Ltd have been prepared on basis that it does not continue as a going concern      8)PY numbers are regrouped/reclassified wherever necessary</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
